+# Veterinarian Free-Text Search Stays Out of Scope, Filtering by Specialty Does Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, on the ground that owner search already demonstrates paged prefix search once. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey.
+
+A request to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty sits on the row's edge. Read one way, NG-9 covers every veterinarian lookup and the request is out of scope. Read another way, NG-9 covers free-text search only, and narrowing a published list is a different capability.
+
+The owner decided the boundary on 2026-08-26.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Read NG-9 as covering all veterinarian lookup.** Rejected: the row's rationale names repeated prefix search as the cost. Filtering on an attribute the directory already prints repeats nothing.
+2. **Withdraw NG-9.** Rejected: free-text veterinarian search still adds a second search surface without teaching a new pattern. Pet search and visit search stay declined too.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 keeps free-text search for pets, visits, and veterinarians out of scope. Narrowing the veterinarian directory by a specialty it already displays is in scope.
+
+The narrowing is bounded by two properties. The filter matches a value the directory itself publishes, and it selects from a list the clinic maintains rather than accepting typed prose. A capability lacking either property falls back under NG-9 and needs its own owner decision.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation as a decided row. Every other row without an ADR remains part of it.
+- REQ-VET-001 and REQ-VET-003 carry the specialty filter. NG-9 no longer contradicts them.
+- Pet search, visit search, and free-text veterinarian search stay declined. A request for any of them reopens nothing by implication.
+- A later filter on an attribute the directory does not display is a fresh owner decision, not an extension of this one.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
