+# Specialty-Filtered Veterinarian Queries Are Not Cached
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+Both read methods on `VetRepository` carry `@Cacheable("vets")`. `CacheConfiguration` creates that cache with statistics enabled and nothing else. Caffeine backs it at runtime with no size limit and no expiry, and no eviction is configured anywhere. [Open Question 5](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey) records that gap.
+
+`REQ-VET-003` and `REQ-VET-001` add a specialty the caller supplies in the query string. A repository method taking that value would key its cache entry on caller-supplied text. Every route in this application is reachable without authentication.
+
+The key space is then unbounded and attacker-chosen. Each distinct string inserts an entry that nothing ever evicts.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Annotate the filtered methods `@Cacheable("vets")` too.** Rejected: it turns an open route into an unbounded heap-growth vector.
+2. **Bound the `vets` cache, then cache the filtered query.** Rejected: it changes eviction for the existing readers, and Open Question 5 has not been settled. That is a wider change than this capability needs.
+3. **Leave the filtered query uncached** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+The specialty-filtered read methods on `VetRepository` carry no caching annotation. The two unfiltered methods keep `@Cacheable("vets")` unchanged.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- No caller can grow the heap by varying the specialty parameter.
+- The unfiltered path is byte-for-byte what it was, which is what `REQ-VET-001` requires of a request carrying no parameter.
+- A filtered request reaches the database every time. The veterinarian list is small, and every vendor schema indexes `specialties.name`.
+- One repository interface now mixes cached and uncached methods. The asymmetry is deliberate, and this ADR is the reason.
+- The pre-existing `findAll(Pageable)` entry is keyed on a caller-supplied page number, which is itself unbounded. This decision declines to widen that surface; closing it belongs to Open Question 5.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-001, REQ-VET-003
+
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vet/VetRepository.java` — the annotated and unannotated methods.
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/system/CacheConfiguration.java` — the cache this decision keeps out of reach.
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the veterinarian contracts and the requirements they serve.
+- [system-design.md § Open Questions from the Survey](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey) — the unsettled eviction question.
